Subject: [PATCH] vLLM 0.25: native W4A16 (Q3VL) via MXFP4_MXFP4 fp4-activation path

Companion to patch 0024 (native W4A8). This is the vLLM-0.25 port of patch 0005
(which fixed W4A16 on vLLM 0.22). It makes the "W4A16 + FP8-last-N" recipe run
natively on vLLM 0.25 + AITER main, instead of crashing at cudagraph capture with
"RuntimeError: Unsupported kernel config for moe heuristic dispatch".

Root cause (verified by git-diffing AITER 883aff7 vs main AND by isolation testing
vLLM 0.22 + AITER main): the AITER a16w4 kernel + its Swiglu-only gate are
byte-identical between 883aff7 and main, so this is NOT an AITER regression. The
discrepancy is entirely on the vLLM side:
  * vLLM 0.22 + patch 0005 reroutes the w_mxfp4 (W4A16) MoE through the MXFP4_MXFP4
    preshuffle layout (rocm_aiter_ops.shuffle_weights + e8m0_shuffle, SEPARATED
    gate/up). With SILU + per_1x32 + SEPARATED, AITER's fused_moe picks FP4
    activations -> the afp4_wfp4 FlyDSL/CK kernel. Fast (fp4 is ~2x fp8 on CDNA4)
    and SILU-native. (So "W4A16" is really fp4-activation at runtime.)
  * vLLM 0.25's rewritten oracle instead lays w_mxfp4 out with shuffle_weight_a16w4
    (gate/up-INTERLEAVED, a16w4) and passes gate_mode=INTERLEAVE. INTERLEAVE + SILU
    routes small-M decode to the bf16 a16w4 kernel, which does NOT exist in the
    ck2stages codegen on gfx950 -> the crash. Patch 0005's fp4-rerouting was never
    upstreamed into 0.25's dispatch.

This patch ports patch 0005 to 0.25:
  * oracle/mxfp4.py AITER_MXFP4_BF16 weight prep: replace the a16w4 interleave
    shuffle (shuffle_weight_a16w4 / shuffle_scale_a16w4 + gpt-oss de-interleave)
    with the MXFP4_MXFP4 preshuffle (e8m0_shuffle + rocm_aiter_ops.shuffle_weights,
    SEPARATED, is_shuffled=True; de-interleave skipped since quark Q3VL stores
    gate/up contiguously).
  * rocm_aiter_moe.py rocm_aiter_fused_experts: drop use_mxfp4_w4a16 from the
    gate_mode=INTERLEAVE condition so W4A16 uses SEPARATED -> SILU picks fp4
    activation (afp4_wfp4), matching the weight layout above. (Leaving it INTERLEAVE
    routes small-M decode to the missing bf16 a16w4 kernel -> crash.)
  * quark_moe.py _setup_kernel: add AITER_MXFP4_BF16 to the is_shuffled=True set.

CAVEAT: like patch 0005, this makes the W4A16 path Q3VL-specific (SEPARATED /
fp4-activation), NOT gpt-oss-interleaved. Serve gpt-oss W4A16 from an unpatched image.

Apply AFTER patch 0024 (both edit the quark_moe is_shuffled block and the
rocm_aiter_moe gate_mode block).

Result (Qwen3-VL-235B, W4A16-base + FP8-last-16, 0.25 + AITER main + 0023+0024+0025):
accuracy_verification_8k Category-F1 = 0.7821 (vs 0.7842 on vLLM 0.22; within 8k
single-run noise; marginal at the 0.7824 gate for N=16 -- use higher N for margin),
offline 7.45 QPS (1xMI350) -- vs 6.64 for native W4A8 (fp8 activations). Serves
natively via afp4_wfp4 (no EMULATION, no crash). See docs/fp8-last-n-runbook.md.

